# The gatekeeper spirits (GatekeeperSpirit): the entrance spirit, talked to by a character in no
# cabal while no cabal owns the Seal of Avarice or wins, shows its own chat window
# (onFirstTalk); the cabal pages are in gatekeeper_spirit_*.scenario. Lilith's death starts the
# exit timer, bound to no NPC and no player, and ten seconds later the exit spirit appears, which
# sends nothing a scenario renders (onMyDying, onTimer): a live expectation counts it. The exit
# line's own spirit stands there from the start, so one spirit is the count before the timer and
# after the despawn, two while the script's stands; it despawns fifteen minutes after it appears.
# Its place (a spawned expectation) is the raid boss's exit point.
trace internal/gameserver/script/testdata/oracle/scenarios/gatekeeper_spirit.golden
character Pilgrim 40
script script.teleport.GatekeeperSpirit
page gatekeeper/31111.htm
page script/teleport/GatekeeperSpirit/
npc spirit 31111 DungeonGatekeeper 10 0 0
npc lilith 25283 RaidBoss 40 0 0
npc exit 31112 DungeonGatekeeper -40 0 0

action spirit
action spirit
  S ActionFailed
  S NpcHtmlMessage obj=spirit item=0 page=gatekeeper/31111.htm
  S ActionFailed
  S ActionFailed
kill lilith
  S SystemMessage id=95 1:0 1:0
  S SystemMessage id=1209
  S PlaySound type=0 file=systemmsg_e.1209 bind=0 obj=0 loc=0,0,0 delay=0
  live 31112 1
  spawned 31112 -
advance 10s
  live 31112 2
  spawned 31112 184446,-10112,-5468
advance 10m
  live 31112 2
  spawned 31112 184446,-10112,-5468
advance 6m
  live 31112 1
  spawned 31112 -
